msgid "What is perf and how do we use it?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/workload-tracing.rst:217
msgid ""
"Perf is an analysis tool based on Linux 2.6+ systems, which abstracts the "
"CPU hardware difference in performance measurement in Linux, and provides a "
"simple command line interface. Perf is based on the perf_events interface "
"exported by the kernel. It is very useful for profiling the system and "
"finding performance bottlenecks in an application."
msgstr ""

